‎## 6. Evidence Separation — Enforced
‎
‎**Per Instrument I-001 — Do not turn signal into hypothesis prematurely:**
‎
‎| Layer | Statement |
‎| :--- | :--- |
‎| **Observation** | Increasing discussion clustering around limits, performance, model availability, migration/portability, and alternative platform choice. PLUS new signal: budget constraint tension — "cutting all AI spend isn't option, neither is bankruptcy." |
‎| **Interpretation** | Users appear to be becoming more conscious of infrastructure surrounding AI relationship, rather than evaluating model solely by output quality. Constraint → Evaluation. |
‎| **Hypothesis — not yet established** | These frictions + budget boundaries may be contributing to broader shift toward multi-platform AI use and greater demand for portability and capability preservation. Needs evidence. |
‎| **Future Test** | Has evaluation produced behaviour? Are users preserving capability vs tool? Are they reducing dependency vs cutting randomly? Need LOGs of actual migration/diversification vs complaints. |
‎
‎**Until behaviour confirmed, log as signal, not migration. Keeps KQ honest.**
